---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Writing guide" noindex>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <p class="index-label mb-2">Your writing workspace</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 dark:text-white">Just start writing.</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">A blank page for your ideas. Give your story a title, then start typing. No sign-in is needed to write.</p>
    <a href="/write/" class="mt-6 inline-block rounded-full bg-accent-600 px-5 py-2.5 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-accent-700">Start a story →</a>
    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Stay in the flow</h2>
      <p>Select text to reveal formatting. Use the <strong>+</strong> beside the story to insert an image, heading, code block, quote, list, or divider. You can also paste or drop images.</p>
      <p>Drafts save automatically on this browser. Open <strong>My stories</strong> to return to one. Use <strong>••• → Download draft backup</strong> to keep a copy on another device. Clearing browser storage removes local drafts.</p>
      <p>Use <strong>Preview</strong> to read your story without editing controls. Your draft remains off the public website until you publish it.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Publish when you’re ready</h2>
      <p>Select <strong>Publish</strong>. Choose Blog, Security Research, or Tools &amp; Projects, then add a short summary, category, and optional tags.</p>
      <p>Connect GitHub with a fine-grained token limited to <strong>cyberpooja.github.io</strong> and <strong>Contents: Read and write</strong>. Create it in <a href="https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new" class="text-accent-600 underline">GitHub’s token settings</a> and enter it only in the connection dialog.</p>
      <p>The token stays in memory for this tab and is cleared when you reload or disconnect. Writing and local drafts do not require a token.</p>
      <p>Select <strong>Publish story</strong> to save it to GitHub. Follow the deployment link to see when the update is live. Images in the story are uploaded when you publish.</p>
      <p>To update a published story, open <strong>My stories → Published</strong>, connect GitHub, and choose the story. Edits remain local until you publish the update.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
